This product is a TypeScript port of parts of PEAR (https://github.com/mit-han-lab/pear),
Copyright contributors to the PEAR project, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
It derives from PEAR at commit f32aa1f7c2ec9c3f45630cc9f8541b3201e8e087: the robot station's agent loop,
its control of the SO-101 arm and the prompt texts they send to a model (pear/agent_loop and
pear/deploy/station). Each source file that ports a PEAR file names that file; the files under
assets/pear are PEAR's own, unchanged unless the README beside them says otherwise.

This product includes the robot description of the SO-101 arm from SO-ARM100
(https://github.com/TheRobotStudio/SO-ARM100), licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0,
as PEAR changed and distributes it (pear/deploy/station/control/robots/so101/description):
assets/pear/so101, and the kinematic chain transcribed from it in src/so101/kinematics.

This product includes software derived from LeRobot (https://github.com/huggingface/lerobot), version 0.6.1,
Copyright 2024 The Hugging Face team, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0: src/feetech/bus.ts and
src/feetech/tables.ts port its Feetech motors bus and control table, src/so101/hardware/follower.ts its SO follower
and calibration file.

src/feetech/protocol.ts ports the packet handler of the FEETECH Servo Python SDK, version 1.0.0
(https://github.com/Adam-Software/FEETECH-Servo-Python-SDK), which its authors released into the public domain
(The Unlicense).

The inverse kinematics step in src/so101/kinematics reproduces, in new code, the optimisation problem that
placo's kinematics solver (https://github.com/rhoban/placo, version 0.9.15) solves when PEAR calls it; no code of
placo is included. placo is Copyright (c) Rhoban Team and licensed under the MIT License.

src/ruckig is a TypeScript port of Ruckig, community edition, version 0.15.3 (https://github.com/pantor/ruckig),
Copyright (c) 2021 Lars Berscheid, licensed under the MIT License: see src/ruckig/LICENSE. PEAR's station generates
its trajectories with it. The order in which the C++ standard library's sort leaves equal elements is reproduced in
new code, written from the algorithm's description; no code of libstdc++ or of a C library is included.

src/agent/clients/openai.ts ports the parts of the OpenAI Python SDK, version 3.35.1
(https://github.com/openai/openai-python), that PEAR's model client runs: its error classes and their messages and
its decoder of a server-sent event stream. The SDK is Copyright OpenAI and licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0.

Where a text the model reads depends on how CPython 3.12 writes a value (the rounding and the text of a number,
JSON, the repr of a string) or names an exception, pear.js reproduces that behaviour in new code (src/python); no
code of CPython is included. src/python/printable.ts holds a table derived from the Unicode Character Database,
version 15.0.0, Copyright (c) 1991-2022 Unicode, Inc., used under the Unicode License
(https://www.unicode.org/license.txt).

